WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.823
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 2: School and Learning.

2
00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.819
This unit is all about school and learning.

3
00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:14.137
You will talk about your lessons, your teacher, and
the subjects you study, like mathematics and grammar.

4
00:00:14.217 --> 00:00:20.688
You will learn the words for the supplies you
use every day, such as an eraser and your books.

5
00:00:20.768 --> 00:00:27.448
You will find out how to get ready for a contest,
write a short report, and use the library well.

6
00:00:27.528 --> 00:00:35.114
Best of all, you will learn to talk about things that
happened in the past — what you studied, where you went,

7
00:00:35.194 --> 00:00:36.717
and why you enjoyed it.

8
00:00:36.797 --> 00:00:42.711
By the end, you will be ready to cheer for
the Grammar Champions in this unit’s story!

9
00:00:42.791 --> 00:00:48.565
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:48.645 --> 00:00:56.343
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name the people,
places, and supplies at school, using words like teacher,

11
00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.651
library, and eraser.

12
00:00:57.731 --> 00:01:04.514
You will also talk about your school subjects, such
as mathematics and grammar, and say which you prefer.

13
00:01:04.594 --> 00:01:11.574
You will also tell about things that happened before,
using the simple past tense (studied, prepared, went).

14
00:01:11.654 --> 00:01:13.992
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:14.072 --> 00:01:19.678
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: teacher,
author, library, graduate, mathematics, grammar.

16
00:01:19.758 --> 00:01:24.150
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

17
00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:27.628
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

18
00:01:27.708 --> 00:01:32.153
The reading sequence includes A Day at
School and Getting Ready for the Contest.

19
00:01:32.233 --> 00:01:32.945
Read actively.

20
00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:36.849
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:40.526
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:40.606 --> 00:01:43.818
The first language focus is The Simple Past Tense.

23
00:01:43.898 --> 00:01:51.391
We use the simple past tense to talk about things that
already happened — yesterday, last week, or a long time ago.

24
00:01:51.471 --> 00:01:54.354
It helps us tell stories and say what we did.

25
00:01:54.434 --> 00:02:01.531
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

26
00:02:01.611 --> 00:02:05.856
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Talk About Your School Day.

27
00:02:05.936 --> 00:02:09.937
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

28
00:02:10.017 --> 00:02:13.044
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

29
00:02:13.124 --> 00:02:16.272
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

30
00:02:16.352 --> 00:02:17.720
You are ready to begin.

31
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:23.952
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

32
00:02:24.032 --> 00:02:26.974
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

33
00:02:27.054 --> 00:02:33.961
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
